# 2. High-Level Architecture

## 2.1 System Layers

The application is organized into five layers. Each layer has a strict dependency direction: downward only.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       PRESENTATION LAYER                        │
│  MainWindow │ TitleBar │ Sidebar │ StatusBar │ Panels │ Dialogs │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                      APPLICATION LAYER                          │
│  WorkspaceManager │ SessionManager │ HotkeyManager │ SearchEngine│
│  ConfigManager │ NotificationManager │ UpdateManager             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                        DOMAIN LAYER                             │
│  ClipboardManager │ TypingEngine │ TabManager │ BookmarkManager  │
│  NavigationManager │ DownloadManager │ BrowserProfileManager     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                      DATA ACCESS LAYER                          │
│  DatabaseManager │ JsonStore │ FileSystemManager │ MigrationRunner│
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                       PLATFORM LAYER                            │
│  WinApi (SendInput, RegisterHotKey) │ Qt Framework │ SQLite │ OS │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## 2.2 Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Responsibility | May Depend On | Must NOT Depend On |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Presentation** | Render UI, capture user input, display state, animations | Application, Domain (read-only), Models | Data Access, Platform directly |
| **Application** | Orchestrate cross-cutting workflows, lifecycle management, coordination | Domain, Data Access, Models, Platform | Presentation |
| **Domain** | Implement business logic for each feature area | Data Access, Models, Platform | Presentation, Application |
| **Data Access** | Read/write persistent storage (SQLite, JSON, filesystem) | Models, Platform | Presentation, Application, Domain |
| **Platform** | Thin wrappers around OS APIs and third-party libraries | OS, stdlib | Everything above |

