## 4.2 Window Manager (`ui/main_window.py`)

**Purpose:** Compose the main application window layout and manage panel switching.

**Responsibilities:**
- Create and own the title bar, sidebar, content area, and status bar
- Manage panel visibility (browser, clipboard, typing, bookmarks, settings)
- Handle always-on-top, opacity, collapse/expand, pin, resize, and drag
- Persist and restore window geometry per workspace
- Coordinate with WorkspaceManager on workspace switches

**Dependencies:** `ui/title_bar`, `ui/sidebar`, `ui/status_bar`, all panel widgets, `core/workspace_manager`, `core/config_manager`

**Public Interface:**

```python
class MainWindow(QMainWindow):
    # Signals
    panel_changed = Signal(str)         # panel_name
    geometry_changed = Signal(object)   # WindowGeometry model

    def __init__(self, app_context: AppContext) -> None: ...
    def switch_panel(self, panel_name: str) -> None: ...
    def set_always_on_top(self, enabled: bool) -> None: ...
    def set_opacity(self, value: float) -> None: ...  # 0.1 – 1.0
    def collapse(self) -> None: ...
    def expand(self) -> None: ...
    def set_pinned(self, pinned: bool) -> None: ...
    def apply_geometry(self, geometry: WindowGeometry) -> None: ...
    def capture_geometry(self) -> WindowGeometry: ...
    def set_workspace_name(self, name: str) -> None: ...
```

**Internal Classes:**
- `_PanelStack` — manages stacked widget for panel switching
- `_GeometryGuard` — debounces geometry save events (200ms)

**Lifecycle:** Created during boot after splash; destroyed on shutdown

**Error Handling:** Geometry restoration failures → fall back to default position and size; notify via StatusBar

**Unit Tests:** Panel switching, opacity clamping (10%–100%), always-on-top toggle, collapse/expand state transitions, geometry save/restore round-trip

