# 15. Error Handling Strategy

## 15.1 Error Classification

| Class | Definition | Example | User Impact | Response |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Recoverable** | Operation failed but app can continue | Clipboard save failed | One operation lost | Retry → Toast notification |
| **Degraded** | Feature unavailable but app runs | Hotkey conflict | Feature disabled | Toast notification with action |
| **Fatal** | Application cannot continue safely | Database corruption | Session may be lost | Error dialog → Graceful shutdown |

## 15.2 Retry Policy

| Error Type | Max Retries | Backoff | Escalation |
|---|---|---|---|
| SQLite busy/locked | 3 | 100ms, 500ms, 2000ms | Toast: "Database busy" |
| SendInput failure | 1 | Immediate | Pause typing; notify user |
| Network timeout (update check) | 0 | N/A | Silent failure (not critical) |
| JSON write failure | 2 | 200ms, 1000ms | Toast: "Save failed" |
| Hotkey registration failure | 0 | N/A | Toast with alternative suggestion |

## 15.3 Fallback Behavior

| Failure | Fallback |
|---|---|
| Settings file corrupted | Regenerate from defaults; backup corrupted file |
| Session file corrupted | Start fresh session; backup corrupted file |
| Workspace database corrupted | Create empty database; notify user of data loss |
| Browser profile corrupted | Delete profile directory; Chromium recreates on next load (user loses cookies) |
| Font file missing | Fall back to system `Segoe UI` font |
| Theme file missing | Apply hardcoded dark theme defaults |
| Icon file missing | Show placeholder square |

## 15.4 Graceful Shutdown

On unrecoverable error:
1. Log CRITICAL with full traceback
2. Attempt to save session (best effort)
3. Attempt to release lock file (best effort)
4. Show error dialog: "batmanoverlay encountered an unexpected error. Your session has been saved. Please restart the application."
5. Exit with code 1

