# 19. Dependency Graph

## 19.1 Allowed Import Rules

```
src/main.py          → src/app
src/app              → src/core/*, src/ui/main_window, src/ui/splash_screen
src/core/*           → src/models/*, src/storage/*, src/platform/*
src/browser/*        → src/models/*, src/storage/*, src/platform/*, src/core/events
src/clipboard/*      → src/models/*, src/storage/*, src/core/events
src/typing/*         → src/models/*, src/platform/*, src/core/events
src/ui/*             → src/models/*, src/core/* (read-only), src/browser/*, src/clipboard/*, src/typing/*
src/models/*         → pydantic, stdlib ONLY
src/storage/*        → sqlite3, src/models/*, src/platform/file_utils
src/platform/*       → ctypes, pywin32, stdlib, PySide6 (Qt types only)
```

## 19.2 Forbidden Imports

| Module | Cannot Import | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `src/models/*` | Anything in `src/` except stdlib and pydantic | Models are passive; they must not pull in business logic or UI |
| `src/storage/*` | `src/core/*`, `src/browser/*`, `src/clipboard/*`, `src/typing/*`, `src/ui/*` | Data layer must not know about higher layers |
| `src/platform/*` | `src/core/*`, `src/browser/*`, `src/clipboard/*`, `src/typing/*`, `src/ui/*`, `src/storage/*` | Platform wrappers are leaf dependencies |
| `src/core/*` | `src/ui/*` | Core must not know about UI (communicate via signals only) |
| `src/browser/*` | `src/clipboard/*`, `src/typing/*` | Domain modules are independent; communicate via `core/events` signals |
| `src/clipboard/*` | `src/browser/*`, `src/typing/*` | Same as above |
| `src/typing/*` | `src/browser/*`, `src/clipboard/*` | Same as above |

## 19.3 Enforcement

Use `ruff` with `I001` (import sorting) and a custom rule or `import-linter` to enforce these boundaries in CI:

```toml
# pyproject.toml
[tool.importlinter]
root_package = "src"

[[tool.importlinter.contracts]]
name = "Layered architecture"
type = "layers"
layers = ["ui", "core", "browser|clipboard|typing", "storage", "platform", "models"]
```

