# 22. Future Extension Points

## 22.1 Plugin System (v1.1)

The architecture prepares for plugins via:

| Preparation | How It Enables Plugins |
|---|---|
| Protocol-based interfaces | Plugins implement protocols to integrate with core |
| Signal-based events | Plugins subscribe to signals without modifying emitters |
| Constructor injection | Plugin services can be injected into module constructors |
| Extensible settings model | Settings model supports `extra="allow"` for plugin config |
| Resource isolation | Plugin directory `plugins/<name>/` contains its own resources |

**Plugin API surface (planned for v1.1):**
- `on_clipboard_entry_added(entry) → entry` (transform or annotate)
- `on_typing_job_created(job) → job` (transform)
- `on_workspace_switched(workspace)` (notification)
- `register_panel(name, widget_factory)` (add sidebar panel)
- `register_search_source(source)` (add to global search)

## 22.2 Cloud Sync (v1.1)

- WorkspaceManager's `export_workspace()` and `import_workspace()` are the primitives
- Cloud sync = automated export to cloud storage + automated import from cloud storage
- Conflict resolution: last-write-wins for JSON; merge strategy for SQLite (TBD)
- Sync adapter protocol: `CloudSyncProvider.upload(path)`, `.download(path)`, `.list_remote()`

## 22.3 AI Integration (v2.0)

- No AI is embedded in v1.0 (users access AI via the browser)
- Future integration point: `ClipboardManager.add_entry()` could trigger an AI summary hook
- Architecture supports this via the plugin system (plugin subscribes to `entry_added` signal)

## 22.4 Localization (v2.0)

- All user-facing strings are candidates for i18n
- Qt's `QTranslator` and `.ts`/`.qm` file infrastructure is ready
- String extraction: `tr()` calls in all UI classes
- Translation files: `resources/translations/<lang>.qm`
- ConfigManager already has `general.language` field

## 22.5 Automation APIs (v2.0)

- Expose a local HTTP API or named pipe for external tool integration
- Operations: trigger typing, add clipboard entry, switch workspace
- Protected by a local-only binding (localhost) and optional token

