# 23. Architecture Risks

| ID | Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| AR-01 | Qt WebEngine Chromium version falls behind, breaking websites | Medium | High | Pin PySide6 to latest stable; test target sites monthly; maintain compatibility matrix |
| AR-02 | PyInstaller produces AV false positives | High | High | Code signing; submit to AV vendors; document in README |
| AR-03 | Memory grows unboundedly with many tabs | High | Medium | Tab suspension after 30 min idle; configurable cache cap; document recommended tab count |
| AR-04 | Workspace switch takes > 1s with many clipboard entries | Medium | Medium | Lazy clipboard loading (paginate); async database operations |
| AR-05 | FTS5 index grows large, slowing search | Low | Medium | Periodic `OPTIMIZE` command; bounded entry count with auto-archival |
| AR-06 | `SendInput` blocked by UIPI in corporate environments | Medium | Medium | Document limitation; detect failure and suggest clipboard paste fallback |
| AR-07 | Circular signal chains cause infinite loops | Low | High | Convention: signals carry data, not commands. No signal handler emits the same signal it handles. |
| AR-08 | Thread contention on typing engine state | Low | Medium | Minimal shared state; `threading.Event` for pause/cancel flags |
| AR-09 | PySide6 API changes in minor versions | Low | Medium | Pin to specific minor version; test with CI on each upgrade |
| AR-10 | Platform-specific code limits future cross-platform port | Medium | Low | All Windows-specific code isolated in `src/platform/`; cross-platform requires replacing this one package |

